ghpull:506 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "auth: document and test Tier 3 (Azure Managed Identity, incoming direction)" ;
    bl:number 506 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:58 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr506 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:58 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-15T13:03:10Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr506Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #58 asked for Azure Managed Identity support so dagalog can validate tokens from other Azure services without a shared secret. Reading sparql_endpoint/src/auth.rs and lib.rs before writing anything showed the generic OIDC machinery from Tier 2 (#57) — AuthConfig::Oidc, OidcConfig::azure(), the --oidc-* CLI flags, and tests/oidc_auth.rs's wiremock harness — already covers this scenario; the incoming direction needed no new validation code, matching AUTH.md's own Tier 3 claim. Rather than stop at 'already done', the plan was checked against how Azure Managed Identity tokens actually behave, which surfaced two real gaps the doc glossed over: OidcConfig::azure() assumes v2.0-format tokens, but classic IMDS issues v1.0-format tokens (different iss claim) unless the resource app's manifest explicitly opts into v2.0 tokens, and assigning an app role to a Managed Identity's service principal doesn't go through the App-registrations portal flow Tier 2 documents. Both are now documented in AUTH.md with concrete fixes, and pinned by new integration tests (accepted/rejected issuer-format cases, missing-role-claim 403) plus a unit test on OidcConfig::azure()'s issuer string — all passing without touching auth.rs, confirming the validator itself was already correct. The separate 'outgoing' Managed Identity direction (dagalog calling Azure Blob Storage) was split into follow-up issue #504 rather than scope-crept into this PR." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:506 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr506Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr506 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr506Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Documented and tested the token-issuer-version mismatch (v1.0 sts.windows.net vs v2.0 login.microsoftonline.com/.../v2.0) that classic IMDS tokens actually produce, rather than treating AUTH.md's 'no code changes needed beyond Tier 2' claim as settled fact once the generic OIDC code path was confirmed to compile and pass existing tests." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered stopping once OidcConfig::azure() and the --oidc-* CLI flags were confirmed to already exist and work in the abstract, and shipping this PR as pure documentation cross-linking with no new tests. Rejected because the plan doc's 'identical to Tier 2, no code changes' framing conflates 'the validator code is reusable' with 'the specific token shape IMDS produces is correctly handled by the documented configuration' — the latter is false without the manifest setting, and following the doc verbatim would have produced silent 401s in a real Azure deployment." .
